#: processes/board-open-close.bpmn:115
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "[x] closes the window back to its avatar. Only a person's [x] does this; a zoom-out never closes a window, or [x] and zooming become indistinguishable to the reader."
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-open-close.bpmn:76
#. Diagram label
msgid "A board is opened"
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-open-close.bpmn:64
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Acts and decides nothing: the start, the gateway and the end all sit in the reader's lane, so every node here is downstream of a choice somebody else made. That split is the point — a renderer that chose what to open would put layout in charge of what the folio asserts."
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-open-close.bpmn:63
#. Diagram label
msgid "Board renderer"
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-open-close.bpmn:34
#. Diagram label
msgid "Board: open and close content"
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-open-close.bpmn:142
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Cards whose rendered width is strictly below the threshold swap to their avatar — automatic, driven by size. Open windows are left alone: semantic zoom and open/close are two mechanisms and must not be conflated."
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-open-close.bpmn:114
#. Diagram label
msgid "Close the window back to its avatar"
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-open-close.bpmn:163
#. Diagram label
msgid "leave"
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-open-close.bpmn:121
#. Diagram label
msgid "Leave a reachable way back"
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-open-close.bpmn:122
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Leave the way back reachable: the collapsed window becomes a control in its own position and focus moves to it — left alone, focus lands on <body> and the keyboard position is lost. An action whose inverse is not reachable is not a toggle (bean l4zi)."
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-open-close.bpmn:159
#. Diagram label
msgid "open a card"
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-open-close.bpmn:99
#. Diagram label
msgid "Project a window onto the board"
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-open-close.bpmn:100
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Project a window onto the board for the chosen card. A window is not the card grown large: it survives zooming out, and only [x] closes it. The frame is fixed ([x] always present, always in the same place); the kind fills in its declared controls."
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-open-close.bpmn:107
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Raise the selected window to the top. Selecting ANY part raises it, not just a title bar. Z-order is session-only by stated default: no z is written to the layout, so a raise is never a file write."
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-open-close.bpmn:106
#. Diagram label
msgid "Raise the window the reader selected"
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-open-close.bpmn:52
#. Diagram label
msgid "Reader"
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-open-close.bpmn:80
#. Diagram label
msgid "Render every card as its avatar"
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-open-close.bpmn:81
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Render every card as its avatar — the starting state. Each content kind controls its own avatar; the board decides only that nothing starts open."
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-open-close.bpmn:162
#. Diagram label
msgid "resize the board"
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-open-close.bpmn:134
#. Diagram label
msgid "Resolve the kind's zoom threshold"
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-open-close.bpmn:135
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Resolve the semantic-zoom threshold for each card's kind: the folio default unless the kind overrides it with a stated because. Return the source alongside the value, so a card that flipped too early can be traced to a decision or to a default."
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-open-close.bpmn:160
#. Diagram label
msgid "select a window"
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-open-close.bpmn:141
#. Diagram label
msgid "Swap cards below the threshold; leave open windows alone"
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-open-close.bpmn:152
#. Diagram label
msgid "The reader leaves the board"
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-open-close.bpmn:89
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Waits on the reader's next action on the board. Opening a card projects a window; selecting a window raises it; `[x]` closes a window back to its avatar; resizing the board re-resolves each kind's zoom threshold; leaving ends. Every branch but `leave` comes back here, which is what makes open and close a toggle."
msgstr ""

#: processes/board-open-close.bpmn:38
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "What a reader does to a board and what the renderer does back: every card rests as its avatar, a window opens onto the one the reader chose, and it closes back to where it came from. You are in this process when the question is a READER's — which card is open, what is raised, how to get back. Semantic zoom is in here too and is deliberately not the same mechanism: the threshold is resolved from the kind and applies itself by SIZE, while opening and closing are a person's acts. Conflating them is how a board starts changing under somebody who did not touch it. The rule the diagram exists to hold is the one about the way back: an action whose inverse is not reachable is not a toggle, and a window that cannot be closed is a navigation dead end wearing a control's clothes."
msgstr ""

